hey guys it's evan i'm here at the soho  conference in vancouver british columbia  and i've just learned about an awesome  new program called dell for  entrepreneurs which provides tons of  resources to help new and established  entrepreneurs grow their businesses so  i'm going to try to corner the president  of dell canada get his take on it and  see what the program is all about and  how can help entrepreneurs  so i've heard this great program that  you've launched del for entrepreneurs  tell me a little bit about it  well evan we launched dell for  entrepreneurs here in canada about a  month ago the program is really centered  around providing entrepreneurs a  platform for enhancing their businesses  and for driving growth and it has a  foundation of four principles one it's  about enhancing engagement and knowledge  around entrepreneurship and how to build  the business two it's about gaining  access to technology what that looks  like what it should be number three it's  around capital providing access to  capital understanding what the different  forms of that are and how they can  utilize it to leverage their business  and then the last one is as you know  very very important access to networks  of individuals that really help a  company move from being that startup  phase to the next phase of growth why  did you want to bring it to canada  what's the incentive behind i got i got  a couple of key areas here number one  i'm a canadian born and raised in canada  i'm passionate about canada and i have  children and my children need businesses  to go into to start up themselves to  work at  entrepreneurs and smbs across canada  represent over half the employment base  i think entrepreneurs really are the  growth engine for canada as an economy  over 500 000 entrepreneurs started  businesses in the last couple of years  and as we look at the future of this  country there's nothing more important  in my mind than entrepreneurs taking it  into the market building their  businesses and really helping canada be  a place that is in the future the place  everyone wants to live i love the  passion coming out but it's great it's  awesome  where does that passion for  entrepreneurship come from so obviously  you're at a huge company dell yeah how  does someone like you as a you know  president for the the company for the  country  how are you still passionate  entrepreneurship where does that come  from hey yeah i do work for dell we're a  very large global company a hundred over  a hundred thousand employees but at the  core and essence of our business is an  entrepreneurial spirit that was  initiated by our founder michael in his  dorm room he started this business and  now it services markets of over 180  countries around the globe  that entrepreneurial spirit is embedded  in everything we do each and every day  we actually have in my performance plan  taking risk as being one of the  components against which i get measured  so  i'm doing  i'm doing okay  but as you look at taking risks that's  really the essence of what entrepreneurs  do each and every day they wake up they  see an opportunity see an area of the  market that's not being served and they  put it all on the line to execute and so  when you look at entrepreneurship that  drives me it drives me for internal  projects that we execute on it drives me  in the way that we engage with  entrepreneurs as young customers of ours  that then grow into very big customers a  couple of really cool examples on that  you may have heard of a company called  salesforce.com  they enable entrepreneurs by effectively  allowing them to get a whole customer  relationship management system at the  push of a button going online getting  that on a web dell was with them at the  founding and we're with them now  providing the infrastructure in the back  end there's another company called  twitter twitter was with dell when they  were a very small startup and now we  work in providing the entire back-end  infrastructure of twitter and the third  one is dropbox we want our files and our  information to be safe and secure and we  work with dropbox to get that done so  the companies that we engage with today  that start from the genesis the kernel  of an idea that then grow and prosper in  the future we want to be with them today  and we know we can scale with them as  they drive growth what's the website and  what do i do when i get hey this is  one of the easiest things that you can  do today it is go on www.dell.ca  backslash entrepreneurs if you can't  spell entrepreneurs then that's probably  an area you should focus on first but go  to that website there we have a number  of areas there to again give you  knowledge give you access to networks uh  help you understand how we can engage  with your capital and then obviously in  today's interconnected world technology  is a part of everything whether it's  engaging with your suppliers engaging  with your customers or helping you go  global with your product your service  your idea so who is this for who should  sign up  evan i would say that any entrepreneur  that is involved in enhancing their  knowledge about how they can really  accelerate their business should start  up for those organizations that are at  that front-end stage of their growth  sign up get on the site  get some knowledge and learning from  other entrepreneurs through the  information that we provided that  education piece is really critical for  those organizations that have  developed their business to the point  where maybe they've received that first  round of funding or they're on the verge  of hyper growth and they're really  utilizing technology to get there we  have an amazing program called the  founders 50 and the founders 50 is a  global program where each six months we  take in  50 organizations we provide them  concierge level service access to the  dell venture fund access to the  engineers within dell and the networks  that we have to really help them get  into that hyper growth stage and so i  think from that end of those that are in  the hyper growth area to those that are  just at the start of their business they  can get great information by going onto  the dell website and accessing the dell  for entrepreneurs program thanks so much  fantastic you're awesome thanks evan  really appreciate it have a good day  everybody
 

